Short:        Squeezebox network music player (AHI)
Uploader:     shadow38
Author:       shadow38
Type:         mus/play
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     68020+, a TCP/IP stack, driver/audio/m68k-amigaos-ahiusr.lha
Distribution: Aminet

amisqueeze turns a classic Amiga into a network music player: a Squeezebox
player for the music servers that speak slimproto, Lyrion Music Server (LMS)
and Music Assistant. The server, its web page or its phone apps see and drive
the Amiga like any other player in the house: play, pause, seek, next track,
volume.

The music comes over the network as an HTTP stream and plays through AHI
(Paula, or a sound card). The server sends raw PCM, or amisqueeze decodes FLAC
itself on a fast Amiga, and MP3 too with an FPU.

Two executables of the same program:

  amisqueeze      any Amiga with a 68020 or better
  amisqueeze.fpu  an Amiga with an FPU (68881/68882, 68040/68060, PiStorm with
                  Emu68): the same, and MP3 decoded on the Amiga

Both run from the Shell or from the Workbench (options in the icon's tool
types), as a commodity.

What it needs:

  - AmigaOS 3.x and a 68020 or better; about 1.1 MB of free memory;
  - a TCP/IP stack providing bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP...);
  - AHI (driver/audio/m68k-amigaos-ahiusr.lha and the driver of your sound
    output, driver/audio/m68k-amigaos-ahidrv.lha for Paula);
  - a music server on the network: Lyrion Music Server or Music Assistant.

user-guide.md, in the archive, tells how to set up the server, install and
run amisqueeze, and what its options and messages mean; CHANGELOG.md lists
the changes of each version.

Free software, MIT licence. Source code, issues and releases:
https://github.com/shadow38/amiga-network-music
